            <ArticleTitle>Special radiofrequency electrode system for computed tomography-guided pain-relieving procedures.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>600-2; discussion 602-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a new radiofrequency needle electrode system for use in pain-relieving procedures. The electrode system is used for computed tomography-guided percutaneous cordotomy, extralemniscal myelotomy, and trigeminal tractotomy. These special electrodes make it possible to perform selective cordotomies and selective trigeminal tractotomies under direct computed tomographic image control.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
